# Force LF on checkout for every text file, regardless of the user's core.autocrlf. Without this, a user whose git has
# core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF on `claude plugin install`, which breaks the shell-script shebangs and silently kills the
# plugin: bin/ongame-launcher → "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" (the MCP server never starts, no ongame tools appear) and
# hooks/browser-check.sh → "env: bash\r: No such file or directory" (SessionStart hook error). .gitattributes overrides
# core.autocrlf, so these are ALWAYS checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit intent for the executables (the extensionless launcher isn't matched by *.sh).
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.ps1           text eol=lf
bin/ongame-launcher text eol=lf
bin/win/*.c     text eol=lf

# The Windows trampoline is a committed PE binary. `* text=auto` above would only need ONE
# autodetect miss to "normalize" line endings inside it and corrupt the executable — which would
# fail as a broken plugin on Windows, not as a visible diff. Marked binary explicitly so git never
# touches its bytes and never tries to diff it.
bin/ongame-launcher.exe binary
